  group_by_underlay, most_diverse_fallback (§73/§74) — wired directly
  into plan.rs's redundant-replica selection
- quality.rs (new): PathQualitySignal/quality_signal_for (§71)
- candidate.rs: PathCandidate gains underlay: Option<UnderlayId>
  (mechanical underlay: None fix across all existing literal
  construction sites: cache.rs, dispatch.rs, estimate.rs, plan.rs,
  privacy.rs, scoring.rs, security.rs)
- plan.rs: redundant-strategy replica selection now prefers an
  underlay-diverse fallback; new integration tests verifying §69/§70/
  §72's route-planning compositions against plan_route's real output
  (one initial assumption about DTN ranking, found false, corrected)
- descriptor.rs: doc-comment cross-reference for §72's stable-
  operation-id/dedup point (no code change)
- lib.rs: mod diversity; mod quality; + updated doc-comment coverage
  map

82/82 tests (up from 71), clippy clean, fmt clean, doc-warning-free.
Zero regressions in siar-dtn-bundle/siar-identity-multidevice/
siar-protocol-ext.
